# Line-ending policy for frozen study artifacts.
#
# 03-PLANNED-TRIAL-MATRIX-450.csv is a byte-exact research artifact: the thesis
# records its SHA-256 (39bb833e0a3af2c7bcbd9c7460119cbac97c324cf07bda4ebcc3b10cfd532298)
# and both scripts/trial-schedule.mjs and scripts/generate-gpt5mini-live-plan.mjs
# refuse to proceed unless the bytes match that digest exactly. Any end-of-line
# normalization (for example core.autocrlf on Windows) rewrites those bytes and
# silently breaks the integrity gate. `-text` disables all conversion for these
# paths so the stored bytes and the checked-out bytes are identical everywhere.
#
# Do not edit the CSV in a way that changes bytes without re-freezing the digest
# in trial-schedule.test.mjs, generate-gpt5mini-live-plan.mjs and EXPERIMENT-STATUS.md.
*.csv -text

# Office binaries: never text-normalize, never attempt a textual diff.
*.docx binary
